+- `setup local` and `verify local` need a Go toolchain, and `tools/agents-infra/go.mod`
+  now declares `go 1.25.5` — the floor its `skill-agents-management` dependency
+  imposes. The generated launcher already needs a toolchain on every invocation,
+  so this is not a new requirement for the runtime, but the version floor is
+  higher than it was: a host below it refuses outright under `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`
+  (`go.mod requires go >= 1.25.5`) and downloads the matching toolchain under the
+  default `GOTOOLCHAIN=auto`, which needs network. A host without Go, or one
+  pinned below the floor with no network, cannot install a local runtime instead
+  of installing a broken one.
 - Setup and `verify local` build to the launcher's own output path, so the
   launcher's first invocation finds an artifact that is already there. Nothing
   is written into the source tree.
